    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="pm_d2">

                <pb facs="pm_d2-1" n="1" xml:id="pm_d2-1"/>

                <head>PM–2. Telegram from the Secretary of State to the Embassy in Panama<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="pm_d2-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">489.</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1958-06-25T19:05:00-04:00">June 25, 1958,
                            7:05 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cur 470.<anchor n="2" xml:id="pm_d2-f2"/> Inform GOP President signed appropriations bill H.R. 12540
                        twentyfifth<anchor n="3" xml:id="pm_d2-f3"/> which included bridge item of
                    $19,250,000. This concludes appropriation entire $20 million for construction
                    bridge which is to remain available until expended and fulfills United States
                    treaty <pb facs="0970" n="882" type="typeset" xml:id="pg882"/> commitment this
                        respect.<anchor n="4" xml:id="pm_d2-f4"/> Department releasing appropriate
                    statement to press.<anchor n="5" xml:id="pm_d2-f5"/> Assume USIS will publicize.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#pm_d2-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="pm_d2-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 911F.7301/6–1758. Priority. Drafted
                    by William E. Price of the Office of
                    Middle American Affairs and initialled by Herbert
                        B. Leggett, Officer in Charge of Central America and Panama
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d2-f2" n="2" xml:id="pm_d2-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; 911F.7301/6–1758.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d2-f3" n="3" xml:id="pm_d2-f3-content">
                <p>For the text of the Department of Commerce and Related Agencies Appropriation Act
                    of 1959 (Public Law 85–469), enacted on June 25, 1958, see 72 State 276.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d2-f4" n="4" xml:id="pm_d2-f4-content">
                <p>Under the terms of the Treaty of Mutual Understanding and Cooperation and
                    Memorandum of Understandings Reached, which representatives of the United States
                    and the Republic of Panama signed on January 25, 1955, the United States agreed
                    to seek the legislative authorization and the necessary appropriations for
                    construction of a bridge over the Pacific end of the Panama Canal at Balboa,
                    Canal Zone. For the text of both the Treaty and the accompanying memorandum, see
                        <hi rendition="#italic">United States Treaties and Other International</hi>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Agreements</hi> (UST), vol. 6 (pt. 2), p. 2733.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#pm_d2-f5" n="5" xml:id="pm_d2-f5-content">
                <p>For the text of the Department of State press release announcing the enactment of
                    this legislation, see the Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, July 14, 1958, p. 68.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
